# No third-party attribution

External inspiration (catalog format, afterRequest timing, size presets, etc.) may
inform behavior. **Never leave fingerprints in the product surface.**

## Never write (new or changed text)

- Other plugins' product names, Korean brand spellings, or kebab/snake identifiers
- Phrases like “like X”, “X-style”, “X analyzer”, “X parity”
- Help/tooltip/changelog/docs/UI copy that cites another plugin
- New identifiers, log tags, prompt lines, or comments that name another plugin

## Prefer instead

- Product terms already used here: Inlay, NovelAI / NAI, Risu `afterRequest`,
  curation catalog, person tags, size presets
- Behavior described on its own (“응답 완료 후 생성”) with no comparison brand

## Existing code

- Do **not** mass-rename load-bearing historical symbols unless the user
  explicitly asks — silent compatibility ≠ new attribution
- Do **not** add fresh third-party wording when touching nearby files
- Do **not** “fix” comments by swapping in another plugin’s name

## Why

Attribution in comments, help, or names makes the inspiration obvious. Keep
implementation quiet; ship Inlay behavior as Inlay’s.
